    <DataNode elementId="AT3G09810-MONOMER" textLabel="Isocitrate dehydrogenase [NAD] catalytic subunit 6, mitochondrial" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT3G09810-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="900" centerY="755" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The IDH-VI gene is predicted to encode a catalytic subunit of the mitochondrially-localized NAD+-dependent isocitrate lyase |CITS:[17468208][14671022][16527867]|. Its ability to functionally complement an &lt;i&gt;idh1 idh2&lt;/i&gt; double mutant from &lt;i&gt;S.cerevisiae&lt;/i&gt; when co-expressed with any of the regulatory subunits (|FRAME: AT4G35260|, |FRAME: AT2G17130|, or |FRAME: AT4G35650|) supports this enzymatic function for IDH-VI |CITS:[16527867]|.</Comment>
