    <DataNode elementId="AT5G09660-MONOMER" textLabel="Malate dehydrogenase 2, peroxisomal" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9ZP05" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="1475" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The cDNA encoding a peroxisomal malate dehydrogenase (PMDH2) was identified and characterized in &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt;. It could be demonstrated that the enzyme is involved in fatty acid &amp;beta;-oxidation through providing NAD to the enzymatic conversion of fatty acyl CoA to acetyl CoA. The enzyme does not participate directly in the glyoxylate cycle as previously discussed |CITS: [17376163]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT5G09660-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT5G09660.4" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Interpro" value="IPR016040" />
