  <Groups>
    <Group elementId="CPLXQT-51" textLabel="NAD+-dependent isocitrate dehydrogenase" type="Complex">
      <Xref identifier="CPLXQT-51" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="600" centerY="835" width="230" height="100" textColor="666666" fontName="Arial" fontSize="10" borderColor="9900CC" borderStyle="Dashed" borderWidth="2.0" fillColor="F5E6FF" shapeType="Rectangle" zOrder="-1" />
      <Comment>The mitochondrially-localized NAD+-dependent isocitrate dehydrogenase is a heteromeric complex in all species studied to date including yeast (&lt;i&gt;S.cerevisiae&lt;/i&gt;), cows, pigs, tobacco &lt;i&gt;Nicotiana tabacum&lt;/i&gt;, and Arabidopsis, though the subunit composition and stoichiometry of the complexes seem to differ between species |CITS: [2198251][16527867][7287723][4319243][9881153]|. The Arabidopsis complex appears to be similar to the yeast complex composed of IDH1 and IDH2 where one catalytic and one regulatory are required for activity |CITS: [2198251][16527867][9881153]|. Arabidopsis has three regulatory subunits (|FRAME: AT4G35260|, |FRAME: AT2G17130|, and |FRAME: AT4G35650|) plus two catalytic subunits (|FRAME: AT5G03290| and |FRAME: AT3G09810|). Any of the six potential dimeric combinations of a regulatory and catalytic subunit can functionally complement the yeast &lt;i&gt;idh1 idh2&lt;/i&gt; double mutant, whereas none of the subunits alone have been shown to complement the double mutant |CITS: [16527867]|. The representative |FRAME: AT2G17130| / |FRAME: AT5G03290| complex shown here contains two of the best-characterized subunits. The exact stoichiometry of the subunits in the complex is unknown and it remains possible that multimeric complexes containing one or more different catalytic and regulatory subunits together may also form &lt;i&gt;in planta&lt;/i&gt; as suggested for tobacco |CITS: [16527867][9881153]|. This enzyme complex is believed to function in the |FRAME: PWY-5690 TCA cycle| and may participate in nitrogen assimilation pathways as well |CITS: [16527867][17468208]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="CPLXQT-51" />
      <Property key="ComplexComponents" value="AT5G03290-MONOMER, AT2G17130-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="ComponentCount" value="2" />
      <Property key="IsComplex" value="true" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-12840" />
      <Property key="GOTerms" value="GO:0005739" />
      <Property key="^citations" value="14671022" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="CPLX-*" />
      <Property key="Locations" value="CCI-MIT-PL" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_16527867" />
    </Group>
    <Group elementId="CPLXQT-49" textLabel="AB-GADPH" type="Complex">
      <Xref identifier="CPLXQT-49" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="900" centerY="835" width="230" height="100" textColor="666666" fontName="Arial" fontSize="10" borderColor="9900CC" borderStyle="Dashed" borderWidth="2.0" fillColor="F5E6FF" shapeType="Rectangle" zOrder="-1" />
      <Comment>This is the major isoform of GAPDH in the chloroplasts of higher plants |CITS: [17031544]|. It is redox-sensitive and subject to auto-regulation, largerly through the activity of a C-terminal extension on the B subunits that resembles the |FRAME: AT3G62410-MONOMER CP12-2| negative regulatory protein. In the dark, under oxidizing conditions, this complex tends to aggregate into inactive A8B8 hexadecamers, according to experiments done in other plant species |CITS: [17031544]|. To date it is unknown whether A2B2 complexes contain GapB with only GapA-1, only GapA-2, or a combination of both. The potential biochemical differences between these putative complexes and the resulting biological importances of them is also not known.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="CPLXQT-49" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase (A2B2)" />
      <Property key="ComplexComponents" value="AT3G26650-MONOMER, AT1G42970-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="ComponentCount" value="2" />
      <Property key="IsComplex" value="true" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-12816, RXN-12815" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="2" />
      <Property key="GOTerms" value="GO:0009507" />
      <Property key="^coefficient" value="2, 2" />
      <Property key="EnzymeNotUsedIn" value="PWY-1042, GLYCOLYSIS" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="CPLX-*" />
      <Property key="Locations" value="CCI-CHLOROPLAST-PL" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_17031544" />
    </Group>
    <Group elementId="CPLX-5301" textLabel="complex II" type="Complex">
      <Xref identifier="CPLX-5301" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="900" centerY="1075" width="230" height="100" textColor="666666" fontName="Arial" fontSize="10" borderColor="9900CC" borderStyle="Dashed" borderWidth="2.0" fillColor="F5E6FF" shapeType="Rectangle" zOrder="-1" />
      <Comment>In mitochondria, succinate is oxidized by the membrane-bound enzyme succinate dehydrogenase (complex II). This enzyme complex is composed of flavin adenine dinucleotide and iron-sulfur proteins. This complex which is not involved in the translocation of protons from the mitochondrial matrix to the intermembrane space, ultimately reduces ubiquinone into ubiquinol. The complex contains two major subcomplexes, the larger, water-soluble, complex contains two subunits: Fp and Ip. The Fp (flavor-iron-sulfur protein) subunit covalently binds FAD and has two iron-sulfur proteins of 2Fe-2S configuration called S1 and S2. The Ip subunit contains an iron-sulfur protein of 4Fe-4S configuration called S3. The other subcomplex is hydrophobic and consists of two small polypeptides. Electrons are transferred from FADH&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt; through S1, S2, S3 to ubiquinone. Complex II is tightly regulated and exists as an inactive form stabilized by binding of oxaloacetate. Incubation with either ATP or ubiquinol activates the enzyme. The inhibitor-binding site as well as the catalytic active site (succinate dehydrogenation) is contained in the larger subcomplex.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="CPLX-5301" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="complex II" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="succinate:ubiquinone oxidoreductase" />
      <Property key="ComplexComponents" value="AT5G66760-MONOMER, AT5G40650-MONOMER, AT4G32210-MONOMER, AT2G46505-MONOMER, AT1G47420-MONOMER, AT1G08480-MONOMER, AT3G47833-MONOMER, AT2G46390-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="ComponentCount" value="8" />
      <Property key="IsComplex" value="true" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-24875, RXN-8981" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="2" />
      <Property key="GOTerms" value="GO:0005743" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="CPLX-*" />
      <Property key="Locations" value="CCI-MIT-IMEM-PL" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_DEY97" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_15604729" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_12374303" />
    </Group>
  </Groups>
